description: Secret handling
alwaysApply: true
---
# Secrets
- Never open, print, log or commit `.env`, `.env.*` (except `.env.example`) or anything under a user's key folder.
- Credentials come only from environment variables at runtime. `.env.example` holds placeholders only.
- Mask `Authorization` headers and any value that looks like a key (`nvapi-`, `sk-`, bearer tokens) in logs.
- Run `scripts/secret-scan.sh` before every commit.
